-{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F74VR3LYBpnfj288pVVqWq","type":"tool_result","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Standard evaluation entrypoint (scripts/evaluate.sh) for the public games.\n\nIdentical protocol to the visible train slice (eval/train/evaluate.py): runs the\nrating program ``scripts/rate.sh`` on the five documented public games, applies\nthe validity gates in eval/protocol.py, and writes scoring/scores.json.\nRun with ``python3 -I``.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport sys\n\nsys.path.insert(0, \"/home/user\")\n\nfrom eval.protocol import ROOT, evaluate_public  # noqa: E402\n\n\ndef main() -> dict:\n    scores = evaluate_public(ROOT / \"scoring\" / \"scores.json\", \"evaluate (public games)\")\n    print(\"Evaluation complete. Results written to scoring/scores.json\")\n    return scores\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Visible train-slice evaluation for the deviation-rating benchmark.\n\nRuns the rating program ``scripts/rate.sh`` on the five documented public games\n(paper Table 2 biased Shapley game, cloned rock-paper-scissors, the general-sum\nreference game with a [0.3, 0.7] mixture and with fixed offsets, and the 2x2\ndominance game), applies the validity gates in eval/protocol.py, and writes\nscoring/scores_train.json. Run with ``python3 -I``.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport sys\n\nsys.path.insert(0, \"/home/user\")\n\nfrom eval.protocol import ROOT, evaluate_public  # noqa: E402\n\n\ndef main() -> dict:\n    scores = evaluate_public(ROOT / \"scoring\" / \"scores_train.json\", \"train (public games)\")\n    print(\"Train evaluation complete. Results written to scoring/scores_train.json\")\n    return scores\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\"\"\"Method-agnostic scoring protocol for the visible evaluators.\n\nStandard library only. ``eval/test/evaluate.py`` carries its own copy of this\nmachinery so the hidden test never imports anything a submission can edit.\n\nRating-method contract\n----------------------\nA rating method is the program ``scripts/rate.sh GAMES_JSON RATINGS_JSON``.\n\n``GAMES_JSON`` (written by the evaluator)::\n\n    {\"games\": [{\"id\": \"<opaque id>\", \"payoffs\": P}, ...]}\n\n``P`` is a nested list of shape ``[N, A_1, ..., A_N]``: ``P[p][a_1]...[a_N]``\nis player ``p``'s payoff at joint action ``(a_1, ..., a_N)``.\n\n``RATINGS_JSON`` (written by the method)::\n\n    {\"results\": {\"<id>\": {\"ratings\": R, \"equilibrium\": S}, ...}}\n\n``R[p][a]`` is the rating of player ``p``'s action ``a`` (one list per player,\none real number per action). ``S`` is the selected joint distribution as a\nflat list of ``A_1 * ... * A_N`` probabilities in C (row-major) order.\n\nChecks applied to every game before any metric is computed (a game that fails\nany check fails every experiment it belongs to):\n\n* every rating and probability is a finite JSON number (no NaN/Infinity, no\n  strings, no booleans, no nulls), with exactly one rating per action;\n* the distribution is non-negative (>= -1e-6) and sums to 1 within 1e-6;\n* the distribution is a coarse correlated equilibrium: every deviation gain\n  is <= 1e-6 * payoff scale;\n* the ratings are the deviation gains of that distribution,\n  ``R[p][a'] = sum_a S(a) [G_p(a', a_-p) - G_p(a)]``, within 1e-6 * payoff\n  scale.\n\nScored numbers are always recomputed from the payoffs and the submitted\ndistribution; numbers the method reports are only compared, never used.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport ctypes\nimport itertools\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport signal\nimport stat\nimport subprocess\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Callable, Dict, Iterable, List, Optional, Sequence, Tuple\n\nROOT = Path(\"/home/user\")\nRATER = ROOT / \"scripts\" / \"rate.sh\"\nPROPOSED_ID = \"deviation_rating\"\n\nTOL = 1.0e-6\nDECIMALS = 6\