 of any rating.\n   - `max_CCE_gap`: worst CCE regret of the base and offset games.\n\n5. **`dominance_preserving`: a strictly dominant strategy is rated higher.**\n   - The evaluator finds every strictly dominated `(player, better, worse)` pair in the game itself. Each game contains at least one pair with a constant payoff gap.\n   - Public game: the 2x2 game where action 0 dominates for both players.\n   - `dominance_violations`: pairs whose rating advantage is not positive.\n   - `min_margin`: smallest ratio of rating advantage to guaranteed payoff advantage. On a constant-gap pair this ratio is exactly 1 for any rating that is the deviation gain of some distribution, so the value cannot exceed 1. It shows whether a method stays in units of payoff, not how far it separates actions.\n   - `CCE_gap`: total CCE regret of the submitted distribution.\n\n### Bystander players\n\nSome hidden games add a player whose payoff depends only on its own action. Such a player does not change the other players' deviation ratings. Its best action has deviation gain 0 under every CCE, though, so the strictest equilibrium of the remaining players is not visible to a single \"minimize the largest deviation gain\" LP. A method must keep selecting among the remaining equilibria to rate them consistently.\n\n## Baselines\n\nAll baselines are computed by the evaluator on the same games, never by the submission:\n\n- `uniform_payoff` (every experiment): mean payoff over all opponent profiles. Its CCE gap is that of the uniform joint distribution.\n- `zero_rating` and `negative_uniform_payoff` (dominance only): constant zero ratings and negated uniform ratings.\n\nOn the public games, the uniform baseline has a Shapley spread of 1.25, clone difference 0.25, mixture drift 0.133333 and offset change 3.0, and violates the CCE condition. The deviation rating reproduction scores 0 on all of these. Baseline rows are reference points and are not subject to the method gates.\n\n## What the test does and does not establish\n\nThe test checks the properties the paper proves (Table 1 and Section 5.1) on games no submission can see beforehand. It does not check which algorithm produced the distribution. Any rating that is the deviation gain of a CCE and is exactly equal on the cyclic games and invariant on these families scores like the reference.\n\n## Packaged scope\n\nThe paper also reports LiveBench and policy-improvement studies. They are not part of the scored benchmark.\n  106 briefing/evaluation.md\n   52 briefing/method.md\n   19 briefing/overview.md\n   36 briefing/problem.md\n   44 scoring/CONSTRAINTS.md\n   27 scoring/DIRECTION.md\n   48 scoring/EXPERIMENTS.md\n   94 scoring/TARGETS.md\n  426 total\n# Experiment Overview\n\nEvery experiment runs the rating program `scripts/rate.sh` on games supplied by the evaluator. The visible evaluators use the five documented public games. The hidden test uses about 190 games that it generates when it runs: 2- and 3-player games, some with a bystander player whose payoff depends only on its own action. Each metric below is the maximum over the experiment's games (dominance violations are summed). Outputs must pass the validity gates in [TARGETS.md](/home/user/scoring/TARGETS.md), or the experiment is scored as failed.\n\n## biased_shapley_augmented\n\nTests whether a method rates cyclic games without forcing an artificial linear order. Public game: paper Table 2 (biased Shapley game plus its Nash mixture N). Hidden games: relabeled, scaled, offset, cloned and populated variants, and versions with a bystander player, plus zero-sum RPS, weighted RPS and RPS-lizard-Spock. In all of them the deviation ratings are provably equal.\n\nScored outputs:\n- `dev_gap`: spread of the first cyclic player's ratings\n- `CCE_gap`: recomputed total CCE regret of the submitted distribution\n- `all_player_dev_gap`: spread across both cyclic players' actions\n- `player_symmetry_gap`: mismatch between the two players' ratings of the same strategy\n\n## clone_invariance\n\nTests whether duplicating a strategy leaves the original ratings unchanged. Public game: rock-paper-scissors with player 1's rock cloned. Hidden games: random games with one action cloned at a random position, with all actions relabeled.\n\nScored outputs:\n- `max_diff`: change in the ratings of the other players' strategies, the ones that face the clone\n- `all_players_max_diff`: change over all original actions of all players\n- `clone_source_gap`: absolute difference between the clone's rating and its source action's\n\n## mixture_invariance\n\nTests whether adding a mixed strategy (weights fixed by the evaluator) leaves the original ratings unchanged and gives the new strategy the corresponding mixed rating. Public game: the general-sum reference game with a `[0.3, 0.7]` mixture for player 0.\n\nScored outputs:\n- `original_max_diff`: largest change in any original rating (all players)\n- `mixture_error`: absolute error between the mixed strategy's rating and the mixture of the original ratings\n- `max_CCE_gap`: worst recomputed CCE regret of the base and augmented games\n\n## offset_invariance\n\nTests whether adding offsets that depend only on the opponents' actions leaves ratings unchanged. Public game: offsets `[[10, -4], [7, -3]]` on the general-sum reference game.\n\nScored outputs:\n- `max_diff`: largest absolute (uncentered) change of any rating\n- `max_CCE_gap`: worst recomputed CCE regret of the base and offset-transformed games\n\n## dominance_preserving\n\nTests whether a strictly dominant strategy is rated above the strategy it dominates. The evaluator computes the dominance pairs from each game. Every game has at least one pair with a constant payoff gap.\n\nScored outputs:\n- `dominance_violations`: number of dominance pairs whose rating advantage is not positive\n- `CCE_gap`: recomputed total CCE regret of the submitted distribution\n- `min_margin`: smallest ratio of rating advantage to guaranteed payoff advantage. It is exactly 1 for any rating that is the deviation gain of some distribution, so it cannot exceed 1","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Fp8njzHn78akq3pLWHhJw3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
