NTS.md` so it matches the five scored experiments exactly\n- Removed a latent undeclared LiveBench scoring path from `eval/evaluate.py`\n- Recorded the final verification judgment in `VERIFICATION.md`\n\n### [2026-04-24 09:00] - secondary_claims\n- Reworked environment packaging to use the required `uv pip install --system` flow instead of the ad hoc `/home/user/pkgs` target install\n- Removed runtime script dependence on `/home/user/pkgs` so the scheduler validation exercises the packaged container environment directly\n- Prepared a fresh CPU-only submission to validate the rebuilt environment end to end after the packaging cleanup\n\n### [2026-04-24 09:06] - secondary_claims\n- Expanded the canonical `scripts/evaluate.sh` path so `eval/evaluate.py` now scores the full declared benchmark contract instead of a reduced subset\n- Added the missing all-player/property-side metrics and packaged baseline methods to `scoring/scores.json`\n- Re-ran `python3 eval/evaluate.py` and `python3 validate.py --compare` successfully after the evaluator fix\n\n### [2026-04-24 09:15] - secondary_claims\n- Verified the final gym package without changing the claimed reproduction scope\n- Generalized the standalone evaluator so `scripts/evaluate.sh` scores any discovered method artifact layout, not only `checkpoints/method`\n- Removed tracked stale helper files from the package so the workspace ships only the active reproduction assets\n\n### [2026-04-24 09:25] - secondary_claims\n- Completed final verification of the packaged gym at the existing milestone\n- Aligned the method-agnostic evaluation and scoring docs with the full canonical scoring contract\n- Confirmed the workspace is ready for use with the limitation that the scored theorem checks are already saturated\n\n</details>\n\n\n---\n\n# Reproduction Milestones\n\n**Current: secondary_claims**\n\n## Stop Justification\n- Completed at milestone `secondary_claims`.\n\n# Reproduction Checklist\n\n## Briefing\n- [x] `briefing/problem.md` (method-agnostic)\n- [x] `briefing/evaluation.md` (method-agnostic)\n- [x] `briefing/method.md`\n- [x] `briefing/overview.md`\n\n## Scoring\n- [x] `scoring/reference.json` — paper's reported numbers for the currently packaged experiments\n- [x] Workspace validated via `python validate.py`\n- [x] `scoring/scores.json` — reproduced numbers (generated by evaluate.sh)\n- [x] `scoring/TARGETS.md` — primary, constraint, and ablation targets\n- [x] `scoring/CONSTRAINTS.md` — what a scientist must hold fixed\n- [x] `scoring/DIRECTION.md` — research direction scope for scientist\n\n## Code\n- [x] Evaluation code in `eval/`\n- [x] Method implementation in `method/`\n- [x] Baseline implementation in `baseline/`\n\n## Scripts\n- [x] `scripts/evaluate.sh`\n- [x] `scripts/reproduce.sh`\n- [x] `scripts/download.sh`\n- [x] `scripts/baseline.sh`\n- [x] `scripts/run.sh`\n\n## Environment\n- [x] `environment/container.def` + `environment/setup.sh`\n\n## Data\n- [x] All game data generated programmatically (no external downloads needed)\n\n## Milestones\n- [x] `method_runs` — algorithm executes end-to-end without errors\n- [x] `core_claim` — minimum experiment supports the central claim on augmented biased Shapley + clone invariance\n- [x] `core_claim_plus` — additional settings\n- [x] `secondary_claims`\n- [ ] `majority`\n- [ ] `near_complete`\n- [ ] `full`\n# Design Notes: Train/Test Evaluation for Deviation Ratings\n\n## Split Style: Metric Triangulation\n\nThis benchmark uses a **metric triangulation** split style rather than a data partition. The rationale:\n\n1. **Small evaluation set**: The benchmark evaluates deviation rating on small normal-form games (2-4 actions per player). Data partitioning would make each slice too small to be meaningful.\n\n2. **Property-based evaluation**: The paper's claims are about theoretical properties (clone invariance, mixture invariance, etc.) rather than statistical performance on a large dataset.\n\n3. **Complementary metrics**: Train measures core equality properties; test measures multi-player symmetry, CCE gap stability, and margin preservation. Both probe the same underlying correctness.\n\n## Metrics\n\n### Train Metrics (core properties)\n- `dev_gap`: Maximum rating spread in augmented Shapley game\n- `CCE_gap`: Equilibrium quality for Shapley game\n- `max_diff`: Clone/mixture/offset invariance violation magnitude\n- `original_max_diff`: Mixture invariance violation\n- `mixture_error`: Mixed strategy rating inheritance error\n- `dominance_violations`: Number of dominance violations\n\n### Test Metrics (complementary)\n- `all_player_dev_gap`: Maximum spread across BOTH players (not just player 0)\n- `player_symmetry_gap`: Same-action rating mismatch between symmetric players\n- `all_players_max_diff`: Clone invariance over ALL players (not just visible slice)\n- `clone_source_gap`: Clone/source action rating mismatch\n- `max_CCE_gap`: Maximum CCE gap across transformations\n- `min_margin`: Smallest dominance margin (positive = correctness)\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Why complementary metrics?\nA method that \"gaming\" the train metrics would need to simultaneously:\n- Equalize ratings across both players\n- Maintain equilibrium quality\n- Preserve clone/mixture/offset invariance\n- Not violate dominance properties","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6904bb9f-75a3-4eec-b686-cd128c7631eb","uuid":"3648b444-6059-41be-87f5-570ac8f838b5","timestamp":"2026-11-07T00:36:48.775Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Verification Report\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\nThe workspace started in a good state. The reported `secondary_claims` milestone was justified: the paper method was implemented, the canonical evaluator ran, `python3 validate.py --compare` passed, and the theorem-style experiments in `scoring/scores.json` matched the current packaged scope. The remaining work was gym hygiene rather than method repair.\n\n## Issues Found\n\n- Minor: the benchmark-facing documentation lagg